.\" ttnr(1) – mdoc(7). Read with: man ./docs/ttnr.1
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt TTNR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ttnr
.Nd text tuner, a terminal player for network radio
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -theme Ar name
.Nm
.Cm play
.Op Fl -volume Ar percent
.Ar target
.Nm
.Cm search
.Op Fl -source Ar id
.Op Fl -limit Ar n
.Ar text
.Nm
.Cm stations
.Op Fl -search Ar text
.Nm
.Cm refresh
.Op Ar target
.Nm
.Cm now
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm ctl
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
plays network radio streams on macOS: Icecast and Shoutcast, HLS, plain HTTP
audio, playlist files
.Pq Pa .pls , .m3u , .xspf , .asx ,
BBC radio with programme and track information, stations of the
radio-browser.info directory and of user scripts.
Audio is decoded by libmpv (FFmpeg) and played through CoreAudio.
.Pp
Without a command
.Nm
starts its terminal interface.
Keys:
.Bl -tag -width "+ = / -" -compact
.It Ic space
play or pause
.It Ic + = / -
volume up / down
.It Ic m
mute
.It Ic n / p
next / previous station
.It Ic s
station list
.It Ic \&/
search radio-browser.info
.It Ic o
open a URL
.It Ic d
output device
.It Ic t
next theme
.It Ic b
line speed of terminal themes
.It Ic \&] / \&[
show track information later / earlier
.It Ic i
diagnostics line (network, download rate, last request, sync note)
.It Ic \&?
help
.It Ic q
quit
.El
.Pp
Keys can be changed in
.Pa config.toml .
Media keys, headphone buttons and Control Center control playback.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm play Oo Fl -volume Ar percent Oc Ar target
Play
.Ar target ,
a URL, a local file, a station id from
.Pa stations.toml ,
or
.Li radio-browser: Ns Ar uuid ,
with one status line per change on standard output until it ends, fails
or Ctrl-C is pressed.
A live stream that drops is reconnected.
.It Cm search Oo Fl -source Ar id Oc Oo Fl -limit Ar n Oc Ar text
Search a source, by default radio-browser.info, and print the stations
with a ready
.Pa stations.toml
entry.
.It Cm stations Op Fl -search Ar text
List the stations of
.Pa stations.toml .
.It Cm refresh Op Ar target
Re-discover the stream URLs of one station or URL, or of all stations,
bypassing the cache.
.It Cm now Op Fl -json
Print what the running
.Nm
plays, or its full status as JSON.
.It Cm ctl Ar command Op Ar argument
Send a command to the running
.Nm :
.Cm toggle_pause , next , prev , mute , quit ,
.Cm volume Ar 0-100 ,
.Cm play Ar station-id .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -theme Ar name
Start with this theme: plain, pdp11-vt100, pdp11-vt100-amber,
pdp11-vt100-green, pdp11-bsd, pdp11-teletype, zx80, zx-spectrum,
bbc-mode7, or a user theme.
.It Fl -volume Ar percent
App volume 0\(en100, independent of the system volume
.Pq Cm play .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , XDG_CACHE_HOME , XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directories instead of
.Pa ~/.config , ~/.cache , ~/.local/state .
.It Ev TTNR_LOG
Log filter, for example
.Li ttnr=debug,info .
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Monochrome output.
.It Ev TMPDIR
Directory of the control socket.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/ttnr/config.toml
settings
.It Pa ~/.config/ttnr/stations.toml
stations
.It Pa ~/.config/ttnr/themes/*.toml
user themes
.It Pa ~/.cache/ttnr/resolve.json
cached stream URLs
.It Pa ~/.local/state/ttnr/ttnr.*.log
logs
.It Pa $TMPDIR/ttnr-<uid>.sock
control socket (JSON lines)
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ttnr play https://somafm.com/groovesalad.pls
ttnr search jazz --limit 10
ttnr --theme bbc-mode7
ttnr ctl volume 40
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mpv 1
.Pp
docs/CONFIG.md, docs/SOURCES.md, docs/THEME-GUIDE.md in the source tree.
